  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Each morning of her five-day workweek, Jane bought either a \\(50\\)-cent muffin or a \\(75\\)-cent bagel. Her total cost for the week was a whole number of dollars. How many bagels did she buy?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Five muffins would cost \\(5\\cdot50=250\\) cents, while five bagels would cost \\(5\\cdot75=375\\) cents. Thus Jane's total lies between \\(250\\) and \\(375\\) cents. The only whole-dollar amount in this interval is \\(300\\) cents.\n\nStarting with five muffins, each replacement by a bagel adds \\(75-50=25\\) cents. To increase the total from \\(250\\) to \\(300\\) cents requires\n\\[\n\\frac{300-250}{25}=\\boxed2\n\\]\nreplacements. Jane bought \\(2\\) bagels and \\(3\\) muffins, choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
